<article class="env-proposition" id="00TN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00TN">Proposition <span data-tag="00TN">10.138.13</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a ring map. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$R \to S$ is of finite presentation and formally smooth, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R \to S$ is smooth. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/031J" data-tag="031J">10.138.8</a> and Definition <a href="/tag/00T2" data-tag="00T2">10.137.1</a>. (Note that $\Omega _{S/R}$ is a finitely presented $S$-module if $R \to S$ is of finite presentation, see Lemma <a href="/tag/00RY" data-tag="00RY">10.131.15</a>.) 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>